ExecStart=/usr/bin/lemonade-server serve
The lemonade-server binary is running itself, and internally it starts the router (lemonade-router) on localhost by default.
That’s why your browser can’t reach it from 192.168.0.11 — it only binds to 127.0.0.1.
✅ How to fix it

You need to pass --host 0.0.0.0 to the lemonade server, so the internal router binds to all interfaces.

Edit the service file:
sudo nano /usr/lib/systemd/system/lemonade-server.service
Change the ExecStart line to:
ExecStart=/usr/bin/lemonade-server serve --host 0.0.0.0
--host 0.0.0.0 tells Lemonade to listen on all LAN interfaces, not just localhost.
Reload systemd and restart the service:
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart lemonade-server
sudo systemctl status lemonade-server
